{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788131566,"nonce":"RPTn518RRqiAeW/5BnqRTVdKwJk=","message":"CLOSED — orchestrator verification, session 4, dorian's Linux box. Merged to\n`main` fast-forward `7e83f9b..28a9fe4` (4 commits). No C# and no `Assemblies/`\nin the range, so no `Build:` commit is owed; I confirmed that with the\nworkspace's own debt test (`git diff -U0 \u003clast-Build\u003e..HEAD -- '*.cs'` minus\ncomment-only lines) — empty.\n\n**Branch-state note, and it is my fault, not the worker's.** I dispatched this\nworker and 2.6's into the SAME checkout instead of isolated worktrees, so these\nfour commits landed on top of `spec/2.6-observer-remediation` while\n`spec/1.4-rwa-cli` sat at `main`. Nothing was lost — the two file sets have zero\noverlapping paths, and both workers correctly refused to \"fix\" the branches\nthemselves. Recovered with two ref moves. The consequence that remains visible:\n**1.4's history sits on top of 2.6's rather than beside it.** I chose not to\nrebase, because 2.6 merged first as a fast-forward (so 1.4's base is simply\n\"main as it then was\") and rebasing would have rewritten the shas this worker's\nown evidence cites. Written up in RUNLOG.\n\nEverything below is MY run. The worker was barred from the game, so the three\nthings it correctly reported as NOT demonstrated are exactly what I ran.\n\n\n    $ rwa ping --pretty\n    pong: true                                                   [exit 0]\n\n    $ rwa status --probe --json | jq .data.health.state\n    \"ok\"        (sends the off-thread `status` verb; answered from the bench)\n\n    $ rwa verbs\n    rwa: 16 verbs; mod root …/AutoRimmer\n    advance digest find-rect journal journal-selftest landmark map-view …\n\n    $ time rwa advance --ticks 3000 --pretty\n    reason: ticks · tick: 248079 · ticks_elapsed: 3000 · avg_tps: 1042.3\n    real 0m3.773s          (2.88s of advance + ~0.9s protocol floor)\n\nExactly +3000 ticks, returns paused. The ~0.9 s gap is the documented\n`PollMs 500` + `MinFileAgeMs 250` floor, and `rwa/README.md` states it.\n\nDocumented jq pipeline, pasted as written:\n\n    $ rwa digest --json | jq -c '.data.alerts.active[0], .data.power'\n    {\"id\":\"Alert_ColonistNeedsRescuing\",\"label\":\"Colonists need rescue\",\"priority\":\"Critical\"}\n    {\"gen_w\":0,\"draw_w\":60,\"gain_w\":-60,\"stored_wd\":1154,\"battery_days\":19.23,…}\n\nNon-zero exit on `ok:false`:\n\n    $ rwa map-view --around 1,1 --radius 99 --json | jq -c '.ok, .error.code'\n    false / \"bad-args\"                                           [exit 1]\n\n\nWith the bench stopped:\n\n    $ rwa status --pretty\n    bench   DOWN  — status.json heartbeat is 19.98s old (stale after 10s)\n      the bench is not running.\n        start it:  cd …/_RimWorld-Agent \u0026\u0026 ./run-agent.sh --quicktest\n        (that is _RimWorld-Agent, the one install an agent may launch — never\n         _RimWorld-Testing and never the MP install)          [exit 3]\n\n    $ rwa ping --pretty\n    ping: rwa-game-down … — command not sent                    [exit 3]\n    $ ls commands/            → (empty)\n\nThe last line is the part that matters and it is a design decision, not an\naccident: liveness is checked BEFORE the write, so a command aimed at a dead\nbench is refused rather than left to surface as `stale-on-restart` at the next\nboot. The message also names the one install an agent may launch and warns off\nthe two it may not.\n\n\nCorrectly, it declined: toggling a workspace on Dorian's live desktop is not a\nside effect a worker's test may have. As orchestrator on that box I ran it and\nrestored the desktop.\n\n    fps before        : 30.0\n    rwa watch on  → {\"action\":\"on\",\"revealed\":true,\"fps_limit\":\"60\",\"hyprland\":\"toggled\"}\n    fps after ON      : 60.1        conf: fps_limit=60\n    rwa watch off → {\"action\":\"off\",\"revealed\":false,\"fps_limit\":\"30\"}\n    fps after OFF     : 30.0        conf: fps_limit=30\n\nThe RUNNING game was re-capped 30 → 60 → 30 with no restart, which is the spike's\nmechanism (MangoHud watches its config file) confirmed end to end through the\nCLI. The window stayed on `special:rwagent` throughout and focus never moved.\nBare `rwa watch` is read-only and reports state without changing it.\n\n\nA 10-command session left `transcripts/20260830T225355/` with `meta.json`,\n`log.ndjson` and one `NNN-\u003cop\u003e/{cmd,result}.json` per command. Replay:\n\n    $ rwa replay 20260830T225355 --run orch-replay --pretty\n    004-advance advance ok · 005-digest digest ok\n    006-map-view map-view FAIL bad-args · 007-ping ping ok …\n    --- 10 sent, 1 failed, transcript …/transcripts/orch-replay\n\nThe one failure is the `--radius 99` command I had deliberately failed earlier —\nreplay reproduces the session including its failures rather than sanitising\nthem, which is what 5.1 will need.\n\n\n    $ cd rwa \u0026\u0026 ./selftest.sh\n      124 passed, 0 failed\n\nRe-run after my own commit below: still 124 / 0.\n\n\nAgainst a live bench mid-advance, `rwa status --sample 3` printed:\n\n    sample  3s: 2699 ticks, heartbeat moved, paused — tick will not move\n                                             without `rwa advance`\n\n`rwa:1056` branched on `paused` first and never consulted `tick_delta` in that\nbranch — so it denied that time was moving in the same sentence as the 2699\nticks it had just counted. That pairing is not a corner: `TimeDriver` pins\n`CurTimeSpeed` to Paused for the whole of an advance and steps `DoSingleTick`\nitself, so paused-and-ticking is this platform's NORMAL driven state. Now four\nstates from (tick_delta, paused) — advancing / ticking / paused / UNPAUSED BUT\nNOT TICKING — with the frame-starved alarm from FINDINGS §4b unchanged. All four\nexercised against a synthetic root. Fixed by me rather than filed because 4.2's\nplay-loop reads this line to decide whether the colony is running.\n\n\n- **The `starved` liveness state against a real frame-starved game — I did not\n  demonstrate this.** It is covered synthetically (a live heartbeat over a\n  flat/slow tick counter) and I saw the live `OK` and `DOWN` states, but\n  producing genuine frame starvation means breaking the render_unfocused fix on\n  Dorian's compositor, which I was not willing to do to his session.\n- **The Windows bench root — I did not demonstrate this.** `rwa root --json`\n  lists it as a candidate; it was never exercised. BORGES can close this in one\n  command.\n- **The Xvfb fallback with the CLI — I did not demonstrate this.**\n- Nothing here was tested under a second concurrent client.\n\n\nThe worker's delivery comment says \"three commits\"; there are four (`28a9fe4`\nswept up the working tree after my branch advisory). Its nine\nDESIGN-vs-shipped-C# discrepancies are real and I have carried the two that\nchange a downstream contract into RUNLOG for Dorian — in particular\n**DESIGN.md §Time model advertises `until:{… condition}` and `TimeDriver`\nimplements `letter|threat|alert|event`**, which 4.2 and 5.1 will both write\nagainst.","files":null}]}